From 81adb7e3e7516ec05e95b6f9cdc5c7a60fb080a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koldfrontier <koldfrontier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:25:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(deepseek-v41): DSML is structure only where its atom is
 the DSML token
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The model writes DSML structure with the ｜DSML｜ token (128825) and spells
a quoted copy, in reply text or inside a string tool argument, in ordinary
pieces. The V4.1 parser matched DSML by text, so a quoted closer ended a
string parameter or the whole call block.
- An argument holding `</｜DSML｜ calls>` came back missing (whole) or
  empty (streamed), still with finish_reason "tool_calls".
- One holding `</｜DSML｜ parameter>` was cut there.
- A reply quoting a V4.1 sample lost it.
See christopherowen/spark-ds41f#948 and #876.

This is a narrow port of vllm-project/vllm#65019 (open, head cad5796ae967)
for this base:
- token_id_scanner.py, incremental_lexer.py and the scanner tests, as in
  #65019;
- streaming_parser_engine.py and parser_engine.py carry token spans
  through lexer tokens, events and each tool slot's arguments;
- parser_engine_config.py gains composite_token_id_terminals;
- deepseek_v41.py makes the DSML atom a token-ID terminal and the six DSML
  terminals composite on it. Argument conversion reads only parameter
  boundaries whose atom is the token;
- whole replies: DeepSeekV41ServingParser.parse sends a reply with output
  token IDs, under auto or "none" tool choice, through the engine's own
  single-pass parse, as a stream already goes. This is the whole-reply part
  of #65019's serving parser. "none" still returns no calls.
  parser_manager selects it for the deepseek_v41 pair.

Not ported:
- the string-argument extender, which this base does not have;
- #65019's streaming re-routing;
- prompt turn boundaries;
- text between tool calls as content;
- metrics and docs.

Without token IDs, matching stays text-based as before. A genuine DSML
token inside a value is still read as structure: that case is ambiguous by
construction.

Tests: tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v41_dsml_provenance.py, with a
mock tokenizer in which the atom is an added token, not a special one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
